ile-search/design-choice-T3SCDB4L.svg" style=3D"color: transparent;"><p><st=
rong>Design choice:</strong> We designed FileSearchCriteria to work alongsi=
de Predicate,
allowing it to evaluate whether a file meets the search conditions without =
handling
all the logic itself. This keeps responsibilities clean and modular. For ex=
ample,
FileSearchCriteria delegates to a Predicate to check if a file=E2=80=99s si=
ze is greater
than 10 or if the owner is =E2=80=9Cbob.=E2=80=9D This delegation enables f=
lexibility. We can change
or combine filtering logic (like checking different attributes or using com=
plex
